# `module::Field::loss_value`

[Back to `module::Field`](../Field.md)

The loss as a plain number.

## Signature

```cpp
double module::Field::loss_value(const pluss::Series &target_prices, pluss::Config cfg = {}) const;
```

## What It Does

The same computation as [`loss`](loss.md) with the result read out as a `double`. [`objective`](objective.md) is the same number under another name; use `loss_value` when you are reading a loss, `objective` when the reader is a minimiser.

## Parameters

`const pluss::Series &target_prices`
: One quote per option.

`pluss::Config cfg`
: Device.

## Returns

The loss.

## Errors

- As for `loss`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A loss as a number.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  const Series prices = field.price().price;
  const Series quotes = prices + pluss::make_series({0.30, -0.20, 0.10, -0.40, 0.25});

  out.writeln("loss =", field.loss_value(quotes));
}
```

### Example 2

Moving toward the quotes lowers it. The made-up quotes are close to a slightly different mean-reversion speed; the loss is smaller there.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};

  mod::Field truth = field;
  truth.model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {2.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04});
  const Series quotes = truth.price().price;
  for (const double kappa : {1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0}) {
    field.model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {kappa, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04});
    out.writeln("kappa", kappa, ": loss =", field.loss_value(quotes));
  }
}
```

### Example 3

The loss choice changes the number, not the minimum, when the quotes are exactly reproducible: at the true parameters every loss is zero.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(12));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};

  const Series quotes = field.price().price;
  for (const mod::Loss loss : {mod::Loss::MSE, mod::Loss::MAE, mod::Loss::Huber}) {
    field.controls.loss = loss;
    out.writeln(static_cast<int>(loss), ":", field.loss_value(quotes));
  }
}
```

